# Backend rules — apps/api (@auraspear/api)

**Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root FIRST**, then this file. The full, authoritative
ruleset (100+ ABSOLUTE rules + every ESLint rule + the security architecture) lives in
`apps/api/CLAUDE.md` — when in doubt, that file wins. Loading order: `AGENTS.md` →
`memory/PROJECT_MEMORY.md` + `memory/TECHNICAL_MEMORY.md` + `memory/SECURITY_MEMORY.md`
→ `context/*.md` → `rules/global/*` + `rules/backend/*` + `rules/security/*` +
`rules/ai/*` → `skills/backend/*` → code + tests → **then** edit. No agent edits first
and understands later (AGENTS.md §0).

Stack: NestJS 11 (TypeScript strict), Prisma 7 → PostgreSQL, Redis (ioredis via the
`@Global()` `RedisModule`), Zod DTOs (no class-validator), OIDC + JWT/JWKS auth,
nestjs-pino logging, Helmet + Throttler + SSRF + AES-256-GCM. Pattern: BFF — the
Next.js frontend never calls Wazuh/OpenSearch/MISP/Bedrock directly; it goes through
this API. Tooling: pnpm only, Node 22. Blocking typecheck is `pnpm typecheck` (`tsc`);
`tsgo` (`pnpm typecheck:fast`) is advisory only. Never work on `main` — branch first.

## Non-negotiable (never violate)

- **No `any`. No `eslint-disable` / `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error`.** Fix the root
  cause. Both are `error`. No `!` non-null assertion, no `==`/`!=`, no `var`, no
  `console.log` (only `console.warn`/`console.error`; prefer NestJS `Logger` /
  `ServiceLogger`). No raw `new Date()`/`Date.now()` — use `date-time.utility.ts`.
- **Tenant isolation is absolute.** Every tenant-owned **query / `update` / `delete`
  is scoped by `tenantId`**. Never `update`/`delete` by `id` alone — always
  `where: { id, tenantId }` (use `updateMany`/`findFirst` when Prisma lacks a compound
  unique). Every repository method takes `tenantId`. Validate parent ownership before
  touching child entities; verify linked/owned IDs (alerts, case owners) belong to the
  caller's tenant (CLAUDE.md #8, #26, #41, #42, #48, #75).
- **RBAC, never bypassed.** **Every endpoint has `@RequirePermission(Permission.MODULE_ACTION)`**
  from `@/common/decorators/permission.decorator`. Permissions are DB-backed;
  `GLOBAL_ADMIN` bypasses in `PermissionsGuard` (never in services). `@Roles()` is only
  for the `role-settings` controller; connector mutations also require
  `@Roles(UserRole.TENANT_ADMIN)` (CLAUDE.md #25, #55).
- **No auth bypass in any environment** — no dev shortcuts, no fake users, no skipping
  JWT verification, no `if (NODE_ENV === 'development') { skip }`. Role comes only from
  the validated JWT — never from client `X-Role`/auth headers (CLAUDE.md #23, #56, #76).
- **No committed/fallback secrets.** JWT/encryption keys + API keys load from env with
  **no defaults** — fail loudly at startup if missing. Only `*.example` files with empty
  values + generation comments; `env.validation.ts` rejects all-zero keys. Connector
  credentials are **AES-256-GCM** encrypted at rest (`encryption.utility.ts`); SSRF-validate
  URLs at input time before storing (CLAUDE.md #24, #53, #59).
- **Prove before deleting** any file/dep/env/route/migration (imports, routes, Docker,
  CI, Prisma, seed, tests, `*.example`). Read → merge → improve, don't overwrite.

## Strict layering (ESLint-enforced — `no-restricted-syntax`)

```
Controller → Service → Repository → Prisma
              ↓
          Utilities
```

- **Controllers** only route and delegate. No business logic, no `try/catch` (let
  `GlobalExceptionFilter` handle errors), no `throw`, no transforms, no inline
  constants/functions. Call ONE service method and return. Guard chain on mutations:
  `AuthGuard → TenantGuard → PermissionsGuard`.
- **Services** are thin orchestrators: validate → call util → call repo → return. **Never
  import `PrismaService`** — data access goes through the repository. No inline helpers
  (→ `<module>.utilities.ts`), no inline constants (→ `<module>.constants.ts`). **No
  method > 20–30 lines**, cyclomatic complexity ≤ 10. Extract every 3–5 lines of cohesive
  logic to a utility.
- **Repositories** are pure data access: accept fully-built params, return raw Prisma
  results. No conditionals, transforms, `throw`/`BusinessException`. **Every method takes
  `tenantId`.** Every `findMany` is paginated (`take` + `skip`, safety `take: 500`);
  every FK / `where` field has an `@@index` (esp. `tenantId`).
- **Utilities** hold all business logic — mappers, transformers, filter builders,
  validators, formatters — as exported named pure functions. No types/enums/constants
  in utility files.

## Declarations have a home file (ESLint-enforced)

No inline `interface`/`type`/`enum`/`const`/standalone-function in service, controller,
repository, guard, interceptor, filter, pipe, or utility files.

- Types/interfaces → `<module>.types.ts` or `src/common/interfaces/`.
- Enums → `<module>.enums.ts` or `src/common/enums/`. **String literal unions are banned
  and raw string literals must be enums** — use `CaseCycleStatus.ACTIVE`, never `'active'`;
  same in `switch/case` and state machines (e.g. hunt `VALID_TRANSITIONS`).
- Constants → `<module>.constants.ts` or `src/common/constants/`. AI agent IDs, OSINT
  source defs, etc. live in constants/enums, never hardcoded.
- Every function has an **explicit return type**. Files are `kebab-case`; full words only
  (`.utility.ts` not `.util.ts`, `definition` not `def`). `node:` import prefix required.

## DTO validation (Zod, not class-validator)

- All DTOs are Zod schemas in `dto/<module>.dto.ts`, validated via `ZodValidationPipe`.
- **Every string field has `.max()`**; **every array field has `.max()`** (unbounded =
  DoS). JSON/record fields (`config`, `metadata`, `parameters`) need a `.refine()` size
  cap (~64KB) on top of the global 1MB body limit (CLAUDE.md #27, #28, #78).
- **Never `@Body()` a DTO type with method-level `@UsePipes()` when `@Param()` is present**
  — apply the pipe on `@Body()`: `@Body(new ZodValidationPipe(Schema)) dto: Dto`.
- **Never `@Query()` a DTO type directly** — NestJS skips Zod on query strings. Parse
  manually: `Schema.parse(rawQuery)`, with explicit number coercion (CLAUDE.md #16, #19).
- Connector configs are validated by **per-type Zod schemas** (wazuh, graylog, misp,
  shuffle, bedrock, …) via `validateConnectorConfig(type, config)` before encrypting.

## Errors, i18n, rate limiting

- **Every exception is a `BusinessException`** with a specific `messageKey`
  (`errors.<module>.<action>`) — never raw `NotFoundException`/`ForbiddenException`/etc.
  Every new `messageKey` must exist in **all 6 i18n files** (`en, ar, es, fr, de, it`).
- `GlobalExceptionFilter` sanitizes all responses in **every** environment — no stack
  traces, internal paths, or Prisma table/column names leaked. It explicitly handles
  `PrismaClientKnownRequestError`/`ValidationError`/`InitializationError` (CLAUDE.md
  #44, #63, #77, #82).
- Apply `@Throttle()` to every mutation/controller. Tiers: auth 5/min, standard CRUD
  30/min, bulk 5/min, delete 10/min, AI 10/min (CLAUDE.md #32, #33, #74, #80).

## Prisma & migrations

- **Every schema change ships a migration.** Use `npx prisma migrate dev --name <desc>`;
  **never edit existing migrations** — create new ones. Test on a fresh DB. For
  permission rows use the `WHERE NOT EXISTS` pattern, **never `ON CONFLICT ("key")`** —
  the unique constraint is compound `(tenantId, key)` (CLAUDE.md #30, #85).
- **Seeds are idempotent** — `upsert` / `findFirst` guard / `createMany({ skipDuplicates })`,
  deterministic UUIDs, per-section try/catch. Safe to run twice and under `start:prod`.
  No fallback `SEED_DEFAULT_PASSWORD` (required env, no `??`). Update the seed when new
  tables need defaults (CLAUDE.md #15, #54).
- Batch DB ops in chunks of 50 via `Promise.allSettled()`; never fire hundreds of
  concurrent Prisma calls. Aggregate with `_count`/`groupBy`, not `findMany().length`.
  Connection pool is bounded (`connection_limit=20&pool_timeout=10`).

## Adding a permission (single end-to-end change)

All atomically (CLAUDE.md #85, §RBAC) — see `skills/backend/add-permission.md`:
backend `Permission` enum → `permission-definitions.ts` (labelKey + sortOrder) →
`default-permissions.ts` → `@RequirePermission()` on the endpoint → Prisma migration
(`WHERE NOT EXISTS`) → **frontend enum mirror + Next.js `src/app/api/.../route.ts` proxy
+ service + hook + UI** → i18n in all 6 locales (feature + `roleSettings.permissions.*`)
→ `npx prisma db seed`. Every backend endpoint the frontend calls needs its proxy route
(CLAUDE.md #86); every sortable column must be in the DTO `sortBy` enum + `buildOrderBy`
(CLAUDE.md #87).

## AI safety (suggest, don't silently act)

AI may **analyze and suggest**; destructive security/infra actions are
`approval-required` and need a persisted `ApprovalRequest` + permission before execution
(CLAUDE.md #97). AI investigation must verify alert tenant ownership (#48). The connector
cascade (bedrock → llm_apis → openclaw_gateway) tries **all** configured connectors
before rule-based fallback — never short-circuit after one failure (#88); no
env-gated mocks (`BEDROCK_MOCK`) in production (#89). Redact PII/secrets before model
calls (`@auraspear/ai` `redact()`); AI memory is tenant-scoped and stores no secrets.
Dispatch automation through `OrchestratorService`; AI listeners are fire-and-forget and
must never block core ops (#31, #32 audit). Deeper rules: `rules/ai/*`, `skills/ai/*`.

## Shared infrastructure

- **Never instantiate external clients directly** (`new Redis()`, Axios, crypto, …) in
  service constructors — inject the shared `@Global()` module (`REDIS_CLIENT` from
  `src/redis`, `PrismaService`, `AxiosService`, …). New infra → make a shared module
  first (CLAUDE.md #29, #33 audit).
- Service logging uses `ServiceLogger` from `src/common/services/service-logger.ts` —
  no inline `logEntry`/`logError` helpers (#34 audit).
- JWT signing/verification pins `HS256`; tokens carry `jti` + `tokenType`; logout +
  refresh rotation blacklist old JTIs in Redis (CLAUDE.md #29, #37, #38, #51).

## Tests & gates

Per module: unit (services/utilities), e2e (endpoints), validation, **RBAC denial**,
**tenant-isolation**, error-path, and seed-idempotency tests. Before claiming done, run
`pnpm typecheck` (+ `pnpm lint`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm test`). Never say "all green" unless
the required gates actually passed; end with the AGENTS.md §13 report block.

